        {
          "id": 2609883986,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I was looking at `wireless_login.cap` but didn't find anything obvious. It's not the value itself which needs to be long, it's the field name being searched for. In the reported crash the field name should have been found in `str` somewhere above 240 bytes, which I don't understand how could happen.\n\nI do find it a bit strange that we truncate with `Label […]: Value` instead of `Label: […] Value`, but that's a different discussion.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
